config ZEPHYR_HAL_REALTEK_MODULE
	bool

config REALTEK_BEE_HAS_PCK600
	bool
	help
	  Selected by SoCs whose HAL drives the Arm PCK-600 power control kit.

	  With PCK-600 every peripheral owns its power and clock control and
	  raises its own active request, its registers are retained across a
	  low power state and its pads switch to their sleep configuration in
	  hardware. Devices therefore only have to release their active
	  request to let the system enter a low power state.

	  Without PCK-600 the platform power manager takes the whole SoC down
	  at once, peripheral registers lose their content and pads have to be
	  switched by software, so devices have to save and restore their
	  context around a low power state.

